        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.412,
            0.745,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By studying the Table 3.1, we can understand how infectious diseases spread and how to prevent them. Here are some simple but important precautions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.471,
            0.62,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Keeping ourselves and our surroundings clean."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.495,
            0.499,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Practising basic hygiene every day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.518,
            0.727,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Washing hands with soap and water to remove pathogens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.542,
            0.726,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Covering our mouth and nose while coughing or sneezing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.565,
            0.699,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Wearing a mask in crowded places provides protection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.588,
            0.599,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Avoid sharing of personal items like towels and handkerchiefs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.63,
            0.566,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Keeping our home, food, and water clean."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.615,
            0.604,
            0.811,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are diseases always caused by infections?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.654,
            0.744,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Staying at home and resting when we are unwell helps the body recover and minimises spreading the disease to others."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.835,
            0.581,
            0.933,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.835,
                0.581,
                0.933,
                0.691
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.696,
            0.746,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some infectious diseases are caused by worms that live inside our bodies, especially in the digestive system. They feed on nutrients and live as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "parasites",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "—organisms that live in or on another living being. These worms usually spread through contaminated food, water, soil, or contact with infected people or animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.801,
            0.695,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4.2 How are non-communicable diseases caused?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.824,
            0.745,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You learnt that non-communicable diseases like cancer, diabetes, and asthma are linked to lifestyle, diet, and/or environment. They are the most common cause of death in India. In Grade 6, you also learnt about diseases like scurvy, anaemia, and goitre,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 18,
